[SF.Seq[1].Main[0]]
TitleExpr = "\"Explanation\""
MessageExpr Line0001 = "\"This examples shows the use of the Multiple Numeric Limit Test step.\n\nIn this example each multiple numeric limit te"
MessageExpr Line0002 = "st step obtains four measurement values \nand compares then to the high and low values below.\n\nMeasurement          Co"
MessageExpr Line0003 = "mparison       Low Value            High Value\nVOLTAGE 0                GELE                    3                      "
MessageExpr Line0004 = "     5\nVOLTAGE 1                GELE                    3                           5\nFREQUENCY              GELE     "
MessageExpr Line0005 = "            110                       125\nRMS                           GELE                  0.5                      "
MessageExpr Line0006 = "  1.0\n\nThere are three steps in this sequence showing three different ways of using a Multiple \nNumeric Limit Test St"
MessageExpr Line0007 = "ep.\n \nThe first step, \\\"Multiple Numeric Limit Test 1\\\", calls a code module that inserts the \nfour measurement v"
MessageExpr Line0008 = "alues into Step.NumericArray one element at a time.  The value for \nVOLTAGE 0 would be placed in Step.NumericArray[0], "
MessageExpr Line0009 = "value for VOLTAGE 1 would be \nplaced in Step.NumericArray[1], and so on.\n\nThe second step, \\\"Multiple Numeric Limit"
MessageExpr Line0010 = " Test 2\\\", calls a code module that writes a \nsingle numeric array to Step.NumericArray rather than writing the four "
MessageExpr Line0011 = "array element \nseparately.\n\nThe third step, \\\"Multiple Numeric Limit Test 3\\\", uses the <None> Adapter and \nther"
MessageExpr Line0012 = "efore does not call a code module. Under the Data Source tab of the Edit Multiple \nNumeric Limit Test dialog box, the s"
MessageExpr Line0013 = "tep has been configured to obtain measurement \nvalues from local variables instead of from Step.NumericArray. The four "
MessageExpr Line0014 = "local variables \nare Locals.Voltage0, Locals.Voltage1, Locals.Frequency and Locals.RMS. The Values \nof these variables"
MessageExpr Line0015 = " are assigned in the Setup step group.\nNOTE: This sequence requires the LabVIEW development system to run.\""

